# Project structure (Pisigo apps)

Website: https://pisigo.com

Prefer a clear layout so agents edit the right files with minimal search:

```
cmd/<app>/main.go          # boot, middleware, DI wiring, Server()
internal/
  http/                    # route registration, handlers, DTOs
    router.go              # Register(app *pisigo.App, deps Deps)
    <feature>_handler.go
    <feature>_dto.go
  domain/                  # business types + ports (interfaces)
  service/                 # use-cases
  repository/              # db/mongo/redis implementations
migrations/                # SQL migrate files
web/ or static/            # optional static assets
.env.example
```

## Routing registration

- One `Register(app, deps)` (or feature `RegisterX`) — avoid scattering `app.GET` across random files.
- Feature groups: `g := app.Group("/api/v1/users", authMW)`.
- Named routes when you need reverse URLs: `.SetName("users.show")`.
- Static: `app.Static("/assets", "./web/assets")` or `app.File`.

## File naming

- `*_handler.go` — HTTP only (bind, call service, map errors).
- `*_service.go` — business rules.
- `*_repository.go` — persistence.
- `*_test.go` beside code; use `pisigotest.GET/POST` for HTTP.

## Dependencies

Pass a small `Deps` struct into registers (db, store, logger). Do not use global mutable clients.
